+    // -X2R / -MR2 / -FRR / -C25SF: THE FAR CELL ON THE EXEMPT 5+ BRANCH (A5, round 5). The same
+    // construction as dcaSplit2 / m3Theta4D2 / t4FarMaxResid, for chains of five or more layers, and
+    // for the same reason: barR is ONE number (-1.2 in barrel and transition, -1.8 elsewhere)
+    // covering every 5+ chain with dcaXY >= 0.5 cm, a population overwhelmingly concentrated just
+    // above 0.5, so a 20 cm displaced five-layer chain must clear a bar fitted on 0.5-2 cm objects.
+    // Above dcaSplit2R the cell gets its own floor m3ThetaR2 and neither the band split nor the band
+    // delta dR applies; the cell also requires a good fit, maxXyResid <= r5FarMaxResid.
+    //
+    // THE GUARD MUST BE RE-FITTED FOR THE LONGER OBJECT AND THIS IS THE WHOLE POINT. With the
+    // 4-layer cell's own value (0.02) this cell is EMPTY -- 34 TCs of 1.6M and zero physics at
+    // breakpoint 5 or 12 -- because a 5-layer Kasa fit over 10 hits does not reach 0.02. At 0.2 it
+    // works: dxy[10,30) +.0025 for fake_barrel +.0019 at (8, 0.2), rising to +.0095 for +.0395 with
+    // the guard removed entirely at breakpoint 5. That is the best efficiency-per-barrel-fake rate
+    // measured anywhere on this band (1.32 against 0.28-0.44 for every alternative), which is why the
+    // mechanism is worth keeping even though the defaults below leave it OFF.
+    //
+    // MEASURED ON 6000 HELD-OUT EVENTS (event_2000 + event_3000..7000), paired against E1-B2 as the
+    // only change: dxy[5,10) +.0034 (p = 9.5e-07, 0 sims lost / 21 gained -- a pure addition), which
+    // takes that band from .2531 to .2565 against LST master's .2549, i.e. from a tie to AHEAD;
+    // dxy[10,30) +.0015 (p = 1.3e-03); vxy[10,30) +.0003; overall efficiency -.0000 (12 sims of
+    // 450,000). Cost, on the holdout where the fake block resolves: fake_barrel +.0019,
+    // fake_transition +.0007, dup unchanged, n TC +1390 and n T4-class **-93** -- it replaces short
+    // output with long output. Both cube samples are at or above B2 on every band.
+    //
+    // The (bill, gain) frontier for dxy[10,30), for whoever tunes this next: barrel fake
+    // (.0019, .0025) (.0087, .0044) (.0191, .0063) (.0395, .0095) with the guard progressively
+    // opened, against a gate CEILING of +.0108. Closing that band entirely costs ~.027 of barrel
+    // fake, which is why this sits at the cheap end and not further out.
+    //
+    // NOT the falsified "maxXyResid ceiling on the 5+ classes" (round 4): that was a KILL for bad
+    // fits applied to the whole class. This is a conditional LOOSENING above a reconstructed-dcaXY
+    // breakpoint and can only ever admit chains. Setting dcaSplit2R = 1e9 restores E1-B2 exactly.
+    float dcaSplit2R = 8.f;
+    float m3ThetaR2 = -1e9f;
+    float r5FarMaxResid = 0.2f;
+    // The C25 (nNodes == 2, nLayers == 5) rule runs AFTER the branch rule and would re-kill a chain
+    // this cell just spared, making the cell a no-op for two-node chains. Worth dxy[10,30) +.0006
+    // for fake_barrel +.0014 on its own. false = E1-B2.
+    bool c25SkipFarR = true;
     // -C25 0.0 / -C25D -2.0 : the (nNodes == 2, nLayers == 5) cell rule; kills only when BOTH
     // margins fail, and never re-kills an already-killed chain.
     float c25Theta = 2.f;
